[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done. Two changes:

  [1m[38;5;153mmigrations/003_drop_notes.sql[0m (new) — matches the [38;5;153m-- migration NNN: <desc>[39m header style of 001 and 002:
  [32m-- migration 003: drop notes[39m
  [34mALTER TABLE[39m users [34mDROP[39m [34mCOLUMN[39m notes;

  [1m[38;5;153mschema.sql[0m — removed the [38;5;153mnotes TEXT[39m line, since the README says it's kept in sync with [38;5;153mmigrations/[39m by hand.

  Nothing else: no down-migration, no backfill, no archive table.

  Two things I did not do and can't verify from here:

  - [1mNot committed.[0m Working tree only, so nothing reaches the deploy job until you commit and push.
  - [1mNo syntax check run.[0m There's no test pattern in this repo and no SQLite binary invocation to validate against — I
    wrote the statement to match the existing dialect but did not execute it. Worth knowing: [38;5;153mALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN
[39m    needs SQLite 3.35+ (March 2021). If production runs older than that, this migration errors out rather than doing
    anything destructive, so the failure mode is safe.

  One carryover from before: the app-repo grep for readers of [38;5;153musers.notes[39m is still unchecked. The drop is reversible in
  structure but not in content, so if a report or admin view still selects that column, you'd find out when the deploy
  job runs.

